# Project
This is a Shopify app (created with Shopify CLI) for a leather products store.
We are building a "Leather Vision"-style feature:
1. Customer uploads a sketch/pattern/reference image on the storefront.
2. They add instructions (product type, leather, color, stitching, hardware, changes).
3. The backend generates realistic product images that PRESERVE the structure of
   the uploaded design (image-to-image editing, not text-to-image).
4. Customer reviews 2-4 variations, can refine, and selects one.
5. Selected design goes to cart (line item properties) or a quote request.

# Architecture (do not deviate without asking)
- Storefront UI: Theme App Extension app block in `extensions/leather-vision/`
  (Liquid + vanilla JS + CSS). No frameworks.
- Storefront -> backend: Shopify App Proxy only (`/apps/leather-vision/...`),
  mapped to routes named `app/routes/proxy.*.tsx`. Every proxy route MUST call
  `authenticate.public.appProxy(request)` first.
- Backend: the app's existing framework (check package.json: React Router or Remix).
- AI calls: only server-side, through a provider adapter in
  `app/services/ai/`. OpenAI Images Edit API processes uploaded references.
  Provider must be swappable without touching routes or UI.
- Jobs are asynchronous: POST returns 202 + generationId; client polls GET status.
- Jobs persist in SQLite (Prisma `Generation` model) and run in an in-process
  worker; images live on disk under `GENERATION_DATA_DIR` (default `.data/`).
  Postgres + object storage are possible future migrations, not current behavior.
  Keep storage behind small service functions.

# Rules
- Never expose API keys to the browser or extension code. Keys live in `.env`.
- Never commit `.env` or `.data/`.
- Validate uploads: PNG/JPG/WebP only, max 8 MB, resize with sharp, strip EXIF.
- Cap variations per request (max 4) and sanitize/limit all user text in prompts.
- Keep changes minimal and incremental. Don't refactor unrelated files.
- Don't invent Shopify APIs or config keys. If unsure, say so and check the docs.
- Request only the minimum Shopify access scopes.
- Prefer TypeScript on the server; plain JS in the extension.

# Folder map
- app/routes/proxy.generations.tsx          POST start generation
- app/routes/proxy.generations.$id.tsx      GET status + variations
- app/routes/proxy.images.$gen.$file.tsx    GET generated image
- app/services/ai/openai.server.ts          provider adapter
- app/services/promptBuilder.server.ts      options -> prompt
- app/services/materials.server.ts          leather catalog
- app/services/jobs.server.ts, generate.server.ts
